WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.780
Fran: I think naming things with
young people is really important.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:13.070
I think there's this tendency when
it's mental health to be like, to

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.265
sort of, work around what you're
trying to say and not say the words.

00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:20.035
And, you know, obviously we deal
with a lot of young people who

00:00:20.035 --> 00:00:22.425
are having suicidal feelings
or they were self-harming.

00:00:22.515 --> 00:00:27.615
And I think there's a tendency in
parents and a tendency in friends and

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:30.825
to be like, "oh, I don't want to say
the word suicide because it might,

00:00:31.395 --> 00:00:32.565
it might make them think about it".

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:36.495
Or "I don't want to say self-harm, you
know, I want to say it in some other way".

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:39.045
And I think as workers, we can
struggle with that sometimes as well.

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:42.630
You know, I was talking to a 14 year
old, like yesterday, who's told me

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.870
he's having suicidal feelings, but
there's even this thing in me when

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.020
I'm talking to him, that I don't want
to say the word suicide sometimes.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.200
But I thinks that's, that's not helpful.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.540
And I think to not name things and
to just be like working around it

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.750
means that you're not actually being
direct with the young person and I

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.330
think they want to feel understood.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.550
And I think they want to
have those things named.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.430
A young person feeling like maybe
you're not listening if you're not

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:09.940
repeating those things back with them.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:14.850
If they're saying "I'm feeling suicidal"
and you'll say then saying, "oh, I know

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.220
you feel down sometimes" then I think
that it can be that sort of thing of

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.380
"well, I'm not telling you I'm down.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.540
I'm telling you I'm suicidal.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.600
So are you're listening to me?"

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.311
And I think it's it's the same
of anxiety and depression.

00:01:24.341 --> 00:01:26.831
So I think sometimes we just
don't name those things.

00:01:27.101 --> 00:01:30.101
I also think a really important
thing about approaching mental

00:01:30.101 --> 00:01:34.386
health of young people is to be a
bit honest about your own situation.

00:01:34.406 --> 00:01:38.786
I think as a therapist is that there's
sort of a few schools of thought, and

00:01:38.786 --> 00:01:43.076
some people think, "oh, you should
keep your, your sort of background and

00:01:43.076 --> 00:01:44.756
your experiences totally out of it".

00:01:44.846 --> 00:01:46.226
I don't really agree with that.

00:01:46.226 --> 00:01:47.947
I think it's, I think obviously
you've gotta be careful, you

00:01:47.947 --> 00:01:48.967
don't want to overshare things.

00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:51.727
You don't want to go into a lot of detail,
but I think for a young person to know

00:01:51.727 --> 00:01:56.407
that I had anxiety or I still have anxiety
sometimes, I think that can make them feel

00:01:56.407 --> 00:02:00.106
really a bit safe in, in the conversation
they're having, and also a bit, cause

00:02:00.116 --> 00:02:02.966
I think they look at professionals and
parents as people who have got everything

00:02:02.966 --> 00:02:07.726
sorted when they're young and then to
hear, "oh no, we're all, we all struggle

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:11.086
with this stuff",  sometimes I think
can be really, really freeing for them.

